<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">You Can Run</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;I just killed Shadow Weaver.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Oh s**t! I just killed Shadow Weaver.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;After Catra fights back against years of abuse, the Fright Zone is no longer safe for her and Adora. Stealing a skiff, they flee for their lives, unsure of what awaits them outside the boundaries of the place they have always called home.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When they meet Double Trouble, Catra and Adora are offered a lifeline - they get a home in exchange for doing a few small jobs. With a vulnerable Catra finally receiving praise for her work, things begin to look up, but as her guilt builds, it soon becomes clear that the shapeshifter has only their own interests in mind.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Can Catra truly escape her past and live with what she's done? Or is she doomed to be taken advantage of again by another abusive authority figure?&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>Alice_h</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
      <dc:subject>
        <rdf:Bag>
          <rdf:li>Fanworks</rdf:li>
          <rdf:li>Explicit</rdf:li>
